# IYDT-GSRP crater analyses

These surface-effects decks infer SUGAR log-yield from two crater response
channels. HOB is not an inferred event parameter in these directories. Each
assessment has fixed-benchmark-yield and errors-in-variables (EIV) variants.

## Analyses

| Directory | Benchmark yield | Type |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `I-EIV-SUGAR-0` | EIV | rapid calibration + event |
| `I-SUGAR-0` | fixed | rapid calibration + event |
| `I-EIV-SUGAR` | EIV | complete joint assessment |
| `I-SUGAR` | fixed | complete joint assessment |

## Native prerequisite

The event-yield prior is under the application `Phenomenology` directory.
From this directory create:

```text
ln -s ../../../Applications/Code/IYDT-gsrp/Phenomenology Code
```

For a rapid case, run `runMPEM.r` in the background and wait for successful
calibration. Always preserve its pristine `.RData` separately (for example, as
`.RData-calibration`) for future event analyses before running `runMPEM_0.r`
in the background. Complete cases run only `runMPEM.r`.

Calibration/complete decks write `opt.RData`. The EIV result seeds EIV
MultiPEM cases and the fixed-yield result seeds fixed-yield cases; use the exact
filenames documented by `../2-Phen-oc/README` and `../4-Phen/README`.

Docker analysis names begin `IYDT-gsrp/Crater/`. A Docker rapid job protects
its calibration checkpoint, but `opt.RData` must be copied from its results
snapshot into canonical MultiPEM inputs before a dependent job is created.

Review EIV, Bayesian, sampler, worker, and seed settings before production use.
